  "file": "README.md",
  "title": "Aeneas",
  "excerpt": "Aeneas (pronunced [Eh-nee-as]) is a verification toolchain for Rust programs. It relies on a translation from Rust's MIR internal language to a pure lambda calculus. It is intended to be used in combination with [Charon](https://github.com/AeneasVerif/charon), which compiles Rust programs to an intermediate representation called LLBC. It currently has backends for [F\\*](https://www.fstar-lang.org), [Coq](https://coq.inria.fr/), [HOL4](https://hol-theorem-prover.org/) and [LEAN](https://leanprover.github.io/)."
 },
